# {{.ProjectName}}

Generated by [api-scaffold](https://github.com/) — a Gin REST API with{{if eq .AuthMode "jwt"}} JWT auth,{{end}}{{if .SwaggerOn}} an OpenAPI spec, and a Redoc docs viewer{{end}}.

## Run it

```sh
go mod tidy
go run .
```

The server listens on `:8080` by default (override with `PORT`).

## Endpoints

- `GET /health` — liveness check
{{- if eq .AuthMode "jwt"}}
- `POST /login` — exchange demo credentials (`demo` / `demo123`) for a JWT
- `GET /me` — returns the caller's claims; requires `Authorization: Bearer <token>`
{{- end}}
{{- if .SwaggerOn}}
- `GET /docs/redoc.html` — API documentation (Redoc), reading `docs/openapi.yaml`
{{- end}}

## Try it

```sh
curl localhost:8080/health
{{- if eq .AuthMode "jwt"}}

TOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST localhost:8080/login \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"username":"demo","password":"demo123"}' | jq -r .token)

curl localhost:8080/me -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
{{- end}}
```

## Adding a resource

From inside this project, run:

```sh
api-scaffold add resource <name>
```

This generates a model, handler, and routes for `<name>`, and wires them into the router{{if .SwaggerOn}} and OpenAPI spec{{end}}.
